            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts opened the argument for Case\u202f07\u2011588."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether the petitioners were arguing that costs should be taken into account."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg questioned how much cost consideration is appropriate and noted concerns about comparing incomparable factors."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether the cost question was merely about the industry\u2019s economic ability to afford the technology."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia inquired whether Section\u202f307 allowed a cost\u2011benefit analysis."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked how cost could be incorporated into the concept of availability."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 58,
              "start": 58
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts queried whether the panel\u2019s decision overruled the prior Riverkeeper\u202f1 decision."
      }
