  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Environmental Protection Agency",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Environmental Protection Agency, the Environmental Protection Agency has for more than 30 years interpreted the Clean Water Act to permit consideration of costs and benefits when setting limits on water intake."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners note that the Executive Branch has required a cost\u2011benefit analysis for regulations for almost 30 years."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Environmental Protection Agency",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 59,
              "start": 59
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Environmental Protection Agency, the EPA argues that the Riverkeeper\u202f1 decision is inconsistent with other opinions and demonstrates ambiguity in the law."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Environmental Protection Agency",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 61,
              "start": 61
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Environmental Protection Agency, ePA\u2019s cost\u2011benefit analysis was not among the most robust forms; it first created national performance standards."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Environmental Protection Agency",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ade17efb97f08f985a290cbdf74a8def3e3af0c314375330f664e90e79f7d002",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ade17efb97f0-0003-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 63,
              "start": 63
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Environmental Protection Agency, ePA also applied a variance when a facility\u2019s costs were significantly greater than the benefits."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
